    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.session\n\n### Description\n\nSession is created with :balt file which opens an empty buffer when I open the session next time. \n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.9.0-dev-135-g96cf385a7\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Open more than one buffer.\r\n2. Close nvim with :q \r\n3. Open nvim\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nNot create the empty buffer file.\n\n### Actual behavior\n\nWe see an extra buffer which is empty. (This is created from balt command saved in the session file).\r\n\r\nMy session options.\r\n`set.sessionoptions                              = 'tabpages,globals,help,curdir,folds,winsize,buffers'`",
